<!-- Tabler "bulb", outline, 24 dp: the SVG from tabler/tabler-icons, path data unmodified.
     MIT, (c) Paweł Kuna.

     The one glyph here that is not a Material Symbol, and the one that therefore gets none of
     the 960-grid treatment the other seven do: Tabler draws on a 24 grid with a viewBox of
     "0 0 24 24", so the viewport is the drawable's own size and there is no group translate to
     move a negative y offset into it. It is also stroked rather than filled — currentColor at
     width 2, round caps and joins — which is Tabler's whole construction and is what carries the
     short rays around the top. See docs/ui.md, "Icons", for why the bulb comes from Tabler and
     the other seven do not. -->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
